        "accordion_dgUc3L": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What type of fabric is best for boat and yacht interiors?",
            "text": "<p>PVC coated fabrics are the preferred choice for marine interior upholstery because they combine the aesthetic appeal of leather with superior resistance to water, UV light, mildew, and salt spray. Unlike natural leather, PVC coated fabric does not absorb moisture, crack in sunlight, or require expensive conditioning treatments. High-quality PVC marine fabrics from manufacturers like Monteiro offer Martindale abrasion ratings suitable for high-traffic yacht areas, while maintaining a soft hand feel and luxury appearance. For interior applications — cabin seating, salon furnishing, wall panels, and headboards — PVC coated fabric delivers the best balance of durability, aesthetics, and value.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_KNPMUw": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How long does marine upholstery fabric last?",
            "text": "<p>Premium PVC coated marine upholstery fabric typically lasts 8–15 years depending on UV exposure, cleaning frequency, and installation quality. Monteiro marine fabrics are backed by a 10-year warranty against manufacturing defects — the longest guarantee offered by any European marine fabric manufacturer. To maximise lifespan, clean regularly with mild detergent and a damp cloth, avoid harsh chemical cleaners, and ensure proper ventilation to prevent moisture build-up in enclosed cabins.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_haK6g8": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What certifications should marine upholstery fabric have?",
            "text": "<p>For recreational boats and yachts, look for fabrics that meet fire retardancy standards (such as EN 1021, FMVSS 302, or IMO FTP Code for commercial vessels), UV resistance testing, and mildew resistance. The fabric manufacturer should hold ISO 9001 (quality management) certification for consistent production standards. For fabrics used in the European market, REACH compliance (EC No 1907/2006) is legally required to ensure no hazardous chemicals are present. ISO 14001 (environmental management) certification indicates responsible manufacturing practices. Monteiro holds both ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 certifications and meets all applicable REACH requirements.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_eXg8Eq": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I order marine fabric samples before purchasing?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Monteiro offers free sample swatches for all marine fabric collections, shipped directly to your studio, design office, or shipyard. There is no minimum order requirement for samples. Samples typically ship within 48 hours of the request. You can order samples directly through the website by clicking \"Add Free Sample\" on any collection page, or by contacting the Monteiro sales team.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_9wyrxF": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is the minimum order quantity for marine interior fabric?",
            "text": "<p>Monteiro offers 1-piece minimum orders for all stock marine fabrics, making it practical for yacht refit projects, prototyping, small vessels, and custom upholstery work. For large-scale OEM boat builder programmes or tailormade development projects, contact the Monteiro marine team to discuss volume pricing and custom production options.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_RBttXd": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How quickly can marine fabric be delivered in Europe?",
            "text": "<p>Monteiro dispatches stock marine fabric collections within 48 hours from its warehouse in Porto, Portugal. Delivery times to European destinations typically range from 2–5 business days depending on location. For urgent projects or large volume orders, contact the sales team to arrange priority shipping or scheduled delivery.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_tGwdpr": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What makes PVC coated fabric better than vinyl or natural leather for boats?",
            "text": "<p>PVC coated fabric outperforms standard vinyl and natural leather in marine environments for several reasons. Compared to basic vinyl, high-quality PVC coated fabric offers superior UV stability, better colour retention, softer hand feel, and longer service life. Compared to natural leather, PVC coated fabric is waterproof, mildew-resistant, lighter, easier to clean, and significantly more cost-effective — while advanced texturing and colour technology now achieves leather-like aesthetics virtually indistinguishable from genuine hide. PVC coated fabric also resists salt spray corrosion, a persistent problem for natural leather in marine environments.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
